From 61dee09df20faa4063d91fc4c3a0dd6af6dda4be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ewan McIntyre <ewan3568@me.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:42:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] Trip builder backend: links can't be pointed elsewhere,
 log in by email, later stages

Security (found in a review of the trip builder):
- A forged Origin header could make our emails point at someone else's site, handing over the crew's
  review key and the guest's key. Links the trip builder builds now only ever use our own sites
  (new trustedBase(); optional TRIP_BUILDER_ALLOWED_ORIGINS for a staging site). appBase() unchanged.
- A trip's link is only stored if it leads to our own trip builder, and the crew's edited version has to
  as well; emails drop any link that isn't plain http(s) (safeHref), so a javascript: link can't be printed.
- trip-builder-request: 5 trips an hour per contact and 10 per address (address kept only as a keyed hash).
- Admin password compared in constant time; a warning while TRIP_BUILDER_LINK_SECRET is unset (set it to
  something long and random: links signed with the admin password could be guessed offline).
- The admin page only makes a trip link a link if it is http(s).

New: trip-builder-login. A guest logs in with the email they used and is emailed a link to each trip they
have sent (signed guest key, no password). The answer never says whether an address has trips; only
paid, live trips; 3 emails an hour per address; an address matches as plain text (no wildcards).

New: later stages of a journey. The builder's "Plan my next stage" sends a new request marked as stage 2+
(payload.stage, summary.stage). The crew email and review page say where they start, where they have
been and which trip came first. Nothing is stored beyond payload: no migration.

Tests: _shared/app-base.test.ts, links.test.ts, trip-builder-stage.test.ts (48 Deno tests in all) and the
end-to-end run (98 -> 114 checks: forged origins, bad links, rate limits, logging in, stages).
See docs/trip-builder-journeys.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
